          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"}>
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2
            \-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} homotopy groups of spheres
            are particularly amenable to study because they are computed in a range by
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+homotopy+theory"} motivic
            homotopy groups via real
            %a{:href => "motivic+homotopy+theory#RealizationFunctors"} Betti realization
            with its Galois action;
          %p
            this is special to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2
            among finite groups, since the Artin-Schreier theorem implies that it is the only nontrivial finite group occurring as an absolute Galois groups. (…)
          %h2#graded_vs_mackey_functor_homotopy_groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} RO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{RO}(G)
            \-graded vs Mackey functor homotopy groups
          %p
            In general, for all real orthogonal virtual
            = succeed "-representations," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi V
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S(V)_+ \rightarrow D(V)_+ \rightarrow S^V;
          %p
            In the case
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \sigma
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
