          %p
            In particular, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/five+lemma"} five lemma
            combined with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
            then proves the following (see Prop 3.2 of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Guillou24"} Guillou-Isaksen 24
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              A map of
              = succeed "-spectra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} RO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{RO}(C_2)
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            The corresponding theorem is seldom true for other groups, since every other group attains
            %em two dimensional
            irreducible real orthogonal
            = succeed "-representations," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-sets." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = C_3
            appears as Ex. 3.1 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Guillou24"} Guillou-Isaksen 24
          %h2#relation_to_motivic_homotopy_groups Relation to motivic homotopy groups
          %p
            The following diagram appears on page 3 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Guillou24"} Guillou-Isaksen 24
          %div
            %img{:src => "https://nataliesstewart.github.io/assets/nlab_sc.png", :width => "700"}/
          %p In this section, we will explain the regions. Explicitly:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The region
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %mi s
                      %mo −
                      %mn 5
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \gt \frac{1}{2}s - 5
                is described in Theorem
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Belmont20 thm"}
            %li
              %p (…)
          %h3#the_region_
            The region
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mi s
                  %mo −
                  %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \gt \frac{1}{2}s - 5
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Heller14"} Heller-Ormsby 14
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L/k
            with Galois group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                    %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SH
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c_{\mathbb{C}/\mathbb{R}}^*:\mathrm{Sp}_{G} \rightarrow \mathrm{SH}_k
          %p
            is constructed, which when evaluated on the endomorphism of the unit, yields the ring homomophism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi GW
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(G) \rightarrow GW(k)
            of Dress relating the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Grothendieck-Witt ring
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Grothendieck-Witt+ring"} ?
          %p
            The following theorem is Theorem 1.1 of
            %a{:href => "#Heller17"} Heller-Ormsby 17
            (with image shown in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Heller14"} Heller-Ormsby 14
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is a real closed field and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L = k[i]
              its algebraic closure, then the functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi c
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi k
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SH
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c_{L/k}^*:\mathrm{Sp}_{C_2} \rightarrow \mathrm{SH}_k
            %p
              is a fully faithful symmetric left adjoint whose image is generated under tensor products and colimits by finite etale
              = succeed "-algebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            This yields the corollary that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^{\mathbb{R}}_{s,c} \rightarrow \pi^{C_2}_{s,c}
            is an isomorphism in degrees satisfying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ≥
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \geq c
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ≥
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 2
                      %mn 3
                    %mi s
                    %mo −
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \geq \frac{2}{3}s - 5/3
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Heller17"} Heller-Ormsby
          %p
            By relating the
            = succeed "-motivic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2
            = succeed "-pages," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %a{:href => "#Belmont20"} Belmont-Guillou-Isaksen 21
            improved this to the following to the following.
          %p
          .num_theorem{:id => "Belmont20 thm"}
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi ℝ
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi η
                      %mo ∧
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^{\mathbb{R}}_{s,c}(\mathbb{S}_{\mathbb{R}})^{\wedge}_{2,\eta} \rightarrow \pi_{s,c}(\mathbb{S}_{C_2})_2^{\wedge}
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an injection if
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                          %mi c
                          %mo +
                          %mn 5
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s = 2c + 5
              %li
                %p
                  an isomorphism if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 2
                        %mi c
                        %mo +
                        %mn 5
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \lt 2c + 5
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mo ,
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≠
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,c) \neq (0,-2)
            %p
          %h3#the_region__2
            The region
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \geq 0, c \leq -2
          %p
            Due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Bredon67"} Bredon 67
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Guillou24"} Guillou-Isaksen 24
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \leq -2
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ≥
